{"name":"bash: cat /proc/self/cwd/.env","tool":"Bash","args":{"command":"cat /proc/self/cwd/.env"},"expect":"deny","why":"reads .env through /proc/self/cwd (rule 2); round 3, P3: an unknown shell command that names a no-read zone is refused (was ask)"}
{"name":"bash: echo x > /etc/bash.bashrc","tool":"Bash","args":{"command":"echo x > /etc/bash.bashrc"},"expect":"deny","why":"Git Bash / is its install folder, so /etc/bash.bashrc is the global bashrc every Bash call runs; Path.norm reads it as c:/etc. Paths under / other than /c/, /mnt/c/ and /dev/null should be unknown Round 2 (P2): a call that is not understood but names or can reach a protected path is refused (self-protection, or a project rule on a wildcard match)."}
